    "description": "How does a great horror film earn an audience’s attention before the story has barely begun? The First Five Minutes of Horror brings together prolific creators from the genre in conversation about what grabs an audience. Using opening sequences from specific films as a jumping-off point, the conversation explores how filmmakers establish tone, character, stakes, visual language, pacing, and genre promise. Confirmed participants: Zach Lipovsky (Final Destination: Bloodlines, Freaks), Eli Craig (Tucker & Dale vs. Evil, Clown in a Cornfield), and Rachel Talalay (Freddy's Dead: The Final Nightmare, Tank Girl, Doctor Who).",
