    "description": "Making its World Premiere at VHS, the Vancouver-shot Encryption is an inventive found-footage anthology from award-winning filmmaker Brayden DeMorest-Purdy. Conspiracy theorist Theo (Alex Zahara: Final Destination Bloodlines, School Spirits) and his niece Eddie (Megan Charpentier: Mama, IT) follow a trail of clues Theo left behind before losing his memory. Their search leads them to a hidden cache belonging to enigmatic tech titan Cryp-Tech, unearthing terrifying analog recordings and mind-bending horrors. Followed by a live in-person Q&A with writer/director Brayden DeMorest-Purdy and cast members Alex Zahara, Megan Charpentier, and Karin Konoval (Planet of the Apes).",
